From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:13:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: apple-dart: leave a powered-down DCP DART
 alone in its IRQ handler

A DCP can power its DARTs down: the internal one for a display
power-down, a T8132 external one (dcpext) whenever nothing is attached
for a few seconds after boot. apple_dart_host_power_off() then marks the
DART host_off, and nothing may use its registers until it is powered up
again. The exception handler did not check that. Its line is requested
shared and is neither disabled nor synchronized at power-down, so an
interrupt for a sharer, or one still pending as the block goes down,
reads the exception registers of a DART with no power. On this fabric
such a read does not fault: it stalls the CPU, in hard IRQ context, and
the other CPUs stop behind it.

Return IRQ_NONE without touching the registers while the DART is
host_off, and wait in apple_dart_host_power_off() for any handler that
already passed the check before the DART loses its power. The handler
works again once apple_dart_host_power_on() clears host_off.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
index 7be0a3ecbe..de28ee8695 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
@@ -4654,11 +4654,17 @@ static irqreturn_t apple_dart_irq(int irq, void *dev)
 	irqreturn_t ret = IRQ_NONE;
 	struct apple_dart *dart = dev;
 
-	if (READ_ONCE(dart->commands_gated))
+	/*
+	 * A DART its DCP powered down (host_off) has no registers to read: on
+	 * this fabric a read of a powered-down block stalls the CPU instead of
+	 * faulting. Its line can be shared or still pending, so leave it alone;
+	 * apple_dart_host_power_off() waits for a handler already past this.
+	 */
+	if (READ_ONCE(dart->commands_gated) || READ_ONCE(dart->host_off))
 		return IRQ_NONE;
 	if (pm_runtime_resume_and_get(dart->dev) < 0)
 		return IRQ_NONE;
-	if (!READ_ONCE(dart->commands_gated))
+	if (!READ_ONCE(dart->commands_gated) && !READ_ONCE(dart->host_off))
 		ret = dart->hw->irq_handler(irq, dev);
 	pm_runtime_put(dart->dev);
 	return ret;
@@ -6843,6 +6849,9 @@ static int apple_dart_host_power_off(struct apple_dart *dart)
 	apple_dart_host_lock(dart, &flags);
 	WRITE_ONCE(dart->host_off, true);
 	apple_dart_host_unlock(dart, flags);
+	/* No exception handler may still be reading it once it powers down. */
+	if (dart->irq > 0)
+		synchronize_irq(dart->irq);
 	apple_dart_pm_invalidate(dart, false);
 	apple_dart_quiesce_commands(dart->dev);
 
-- 
2.43.0

